  VERDICT: median |dev| 1.00c -> 3.00c at mid.
  -> The mid estimate is LARGER than the last-trade one, which no
     unbiased mid can be. The mid is contaminated, almost always by
     cross-leg non-simultaneity: summing per-leg daily statistics
     taken at different times of day does not produce a basket.
     Re-run with --max-basket-span to force the legs to be
     contemporaneous before reading anything into the mid rows.
     Until then, read the ASK and BID rows, not the MID rows.

  EXECUTABLE READING (no mid required):
    buying every leg at the ask  costs  $1.1334 per basket
    selling every leg at the bid yields $0.9993 per basket
    a basket settles at exactly $1.00.
    -> Selling at the bid nets -0.07c gross: ZERO edge before
